   260	## 10. Residual risks
   261	- **Retrieval thresholds.** Tier 3 thresholds for retrieval (10 % of P1's Δ_C4 ≈ 3.5–6.8 items) are within numerical jitter, so `pass_c4` on R@k may turn on 1–2 item flips. It is reported as registered.
   262	- **E2 at K8** compares against a neuronic cell.
   263	- **B-F timing.** Co-tenant times for B-F cells have not been measured on this box since August, so the ETA range stays wide until chunks 3–4.
   264	- **NAS stalls.** The NAS (CIFS) can stall; any item substitution is caught by `--expected-stream-count` and the registry.
   265	- **exp_22 dependency.** exp_22's backend amendment and its watcher's reservation support belong to an exp_22 round (decision 7), not to exp_35 code. The exp_22 watcher stays suspended until then.
